Work Log Details
T001 — Project Setup

The Smart Stock Savvy project was initialized using Lovable. The initial project structure, frontend environment and application configuration were established by Eeshani.

T002 — UI and Navigation

Shrinjini designed the main navigation structure and user interface for the inventory management system. The interface was designed to allow users to access inventory information and management functions easily.

T003 — Authentication

Eeshani implemented the authentication interface to provide controlled access to the application and help prevent unauthorized users from accessing protected inventory functionality.

T004 — Inventory Dashboard

Shrinjini created the main inventory dashboard, providing users with a centralized view of stock information and important inventory indicators.

T005 — Database Structure

Sujishnu designed the inventory data model to support products, categories, users, stock quantities and inventory transactions.

T006 — Product Management

Sujishnu implemented product management functionality, allowing authorized users to add and modify inventory information.

T007 — Stock Tracking

Raibat implemented stock quantity tracking so that the system can maintain current product quantities and reflect inventory changes.

T008 — Low-Stock Identification

Raibat implemented the identification of products whose stock levels fall below the required threshold. This helps users identify products that may require replenishment.

T009 — Search and Filtering

Shrinjini implemented search and filtering functionality to allow users to locate relevant inventory records efficiently.

T010 — Dashboard Analytics

Thiruharan incorporated inventory statistics and summaries into the dashboard to provide users with a quick overview of the current inventory situation.

T011 — Frontend and Backend Integration

Sujishnu connected the frontend components with the backend/data layer so that application operations could work with persistent inventory information.

T012 — Functional Testing

Raibat tested important inventory operations, including product creation, editing and stock updates.

T013 — Authentication Testing

Eeshani tested the authentication-related functionality to verify that the login and protected application flow operated correctly.

T014 — UI Improvements

Shrinjini reviewed and improved the interface for usability, consistency and responsiveness. Issues identified during testing were corrected where possible.

T015 — Deployment

Thiruharan was responsible for deploying and publishing the application as a live web application.

Current published application:

https://smart-stock-savvy-47.lovable.app

T016 — Cloud Architecture

Thiruharan designed a scalable cloud deployment architecture using AWS services including Amazon S3, CloudFront, AWS WAF, Application Load Balancer, ECS/Fargate, RDS PostgreSQL, ElastiCache and SQS.

T017 — Architecture Documentation

Eeshani documented the current system architecture and proposed AWS cloud architecture in architecture.md.

T018 — Final Testing

All five students participated in final testing of the completed application using the published deployment to verify the main user interface and inventory-management workflow.

T019 — Remaining Issues

Raibat and Sujishnu are reviewing the application for remaining bugs, technical issues and possible improvements before final submission.

T020 — Final Documentation

All five students are contributing to the required project documentation, architecture documentation, implementation log and final submission materials.

